When he noticed two citizens who stood a little separately from the crowd, he decided to eavesdrop on their conversation. Ragnar approached as close as possible and pretended to be reading the announcement.
"They say the chamberlain is offering a huge amount of money," lisped the first one.
"No one can earn that money," hemmed the other one.
"Well, someone has got to kill this monster, or we might run out of water one day," sighed the lisping one.
"Yeah, but there is no one foolish enough to do it. Would you go?"
"Me?! No, I can't, I...."
Ragnar didn't hear the end of the conversation. He had gotten information he needed and decided to go to the chamberlain without delay.